  "limitations": [
    "Reverts with invalid signatures show that both EIP-3009 overloads reach signature validation. They are not successful transfer tests or proof of end-to-end x402 interoperability.",
    "DOMAIN_SEPARATOR values were recomputed locally for name, version, chain ID, and token address; equality confirms those domain inputs at the observed state.",
    "USDC and EURC eth_getCode results are proxy runtime code. Code presence and published ABI alone do not establish full wallet-signature compatibility.",
    "The universal validator address used by the current EIP-6492 path has no code. This does not block ordinary EOA authorizations, which use a different path.",
    "The public facilitator testnet address had zero native and ERC-20 USDC balance. A funded test fixture is required for future settlement tests.",
    "Native and ERC-20 USDC expose one balance at different precision; ERC-20 balance is the native balance divided by 10^12 with integer truncation.",
    "Circle Gateway Arc exact uses GatewayWalletBatched v1 and pending batched settlement; it is a different payment method from direct token EIP-3009 despite sharing scheme and network.",
    "Documentation and endpoint capabilities can change; refresh deployment data and dependencies before implementing or launching mainnet."
  ]
}
